    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Equations A3.21a,b provide the framework for constructing equivalent models, and hence obtaining models that are potentially easier to analyze. Consider the situation where our interest is in the prediction of random effects and we wish to obtain an equivalent model that considers the same fixed effects but uses a different vector of random effects. (For example, instead of considering a vector of both parental and offspring breeding values, we might simply consider the vector of parental breeding values, using the parental estimates to subsequently estimate the breeding values in their offspring.) If the original model is",
